    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: SBQQ__ConfigurationAttribute__c records with no SBQQ__TargetField__c set.
Why it matters: The attribute appears in the configurator but its value goes nowhere — pricing rules and product rules can&apos;t read it. Sales reps fill in data thinking it matters; pricing engine ignores it.
Suppress a finding: when the attribute is intentionally display-only and downstream automation reads it directly via the standard CPQ attribute storage.
Disable the detector: only if your org doesn&apos;t use configuration attributes. Most CPQ orgs should leave this on.</value></values>
